SDL3: write the MSVC `_alloca in malloc.h` test source into the binary dir, not the source tree

SDL's root CMakeLists.txt checks for `_alloca` with a hand-written try_compile, because
CheckSymbolExists cannot see an intrinsic. It wrote the test source to
${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/test_malloc_alloca.c, so a configure with MSVC or clang-cl put
an untracked file into third_party/sdl3/SDL3-3.4.18/. That dirties the checkout, and
`vendor.py verify` fails on it ("unexpected file"). The check runs on the first configure of a
build directory whenever SDL does not preseed the MSVC cache (SDL_PRESEED off, or its
CAN_PRESEED probe fails); a preseeded cache already holds _ALLOCA_IN_MALLOC_H.

The patch writes the file to ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}, next to the try_compile directory the
check already uses there. The check and its result do not change.

Engine-local patch (DENG-367), applied by tools/vendor/vendor.py. Drop it when a pinned SDL
release writes this file outside the source tree.

diff --git a/SDL3-3.4.18/CMakeLists.txt b/SDL3-3.4.18/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/SDL3-3.4.18/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/SDL3-3.4.18/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1029,7 +1029,7 @@ if(MSVC)
   # Cannot use CheckSymbolExists for _alloca: purely intrinsic functions have no address (C7552)
   if(NOT DEFINED _ALLOCA_IN_MALLOC_H)
     message(STATUS "Looking for _alloca in malloc.h")
-    set(testsrc "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/test_malloc_alloca.c")
+    set(testsrc "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/test_malloc_alloca.c")
     file(WRITE "${testsrc}" "#include <malloc.h>\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]) { void *ptr = _alloca(argc * (int)argv[0][0]); return ptr != (void *)0; }")
     try_compile(_ALLOCA_IN_MALLOC_H "${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/alloca_in_malloc_h" SOURCES "${testsrc}")
     message(STATUS "Looking for _alloca in malloc.h - ${_ALLOCA_IN_MALLOC_H}")
